=== Stat Order Optimization ===

[[Planet_Shop#Redistribution|Redistributing]] a zodiac rerolls the zodiac sign within the zodiac element an also shuffles around its stat order. This is very important because the stat order has a major effect on the stat values. The top stat gets a significant boost while the bottom stat receives a major penalty. By repeatedly redistributing a zodiac, you can make sure that all your zodiacs have the stats that really matter on top and the ones that don't matter at the bottom for a noticeable boost to your overall strength.

Every time you merge, the stat order gets shuffled around, so as long as you keep switching out and upgrading your zodiacs, you probably should only bother about top stat. It can take a lot of rerolls for that "perfect" order. Also note that even later on, going further than just for top stat will yield a very small difference. Both zodiac stats and overall effects may be softcapped and testing on the actual optimality of the presented stat order beyond top stat has been spotty at best.

Stat Priorities:

<pre>
Aqua: DP -> SN -> LL -> FL
Libra: DP -> SN -> EP / LL
Gemini: ET -> SN -> EP / LL

Aries: Exp -> Asc / Prom / Mult
Leo: Exp -> Asc / Prom / LS

Canc: Center -> Ach29 / GS -> DTP
Scorp: Luck -> Center -> Ach29 / GS
Pisc: Qual -> Luck -> Ach29 / GS
</pre>

=== Enhancing ===

Once you have reached the point where you are unlikely to further improve your zodiacs by farming/merging, you have probably spent hours on each zodiac. At this point, you might as well go the extra mile and spend some Astrodust on enhancing these zodiacs for a further tiny bit of stat gains. With minerals, only enhance with Sword Lv.50. This is what makes it good again.

Know that while stat order is not affected by enhancing, every time you successfully enhance a zodiac, there will be a hidden quality roll that affects stat values. A good roll will give you a big stat boost, while a bad roll might even decrease stats. 

For optimal results, keep an eye on the enhancing costs. A good roll will be noticeable by observing a jump in enhancing costs, while a bad roll will barely increase or even decrease the cost a bit.

You will need a lot of Astrodust and an autoclicker for this process since success rates are abysmal and you will need a lot of successes to see a meaningful difference to stats.

For a reference of how much Astrodust is approximately needed, here's the formula for Enhance Price and Success Chance:

<pre>
Zodiac Enhance Price  = ZodiacSellCost * 2 * 1.3^log(1 + ZodiacQuality)
Zodiac Enhance Chance = 0.9^(log(1 + ZodiacQuality)^2) * 100%

where:
Zodiac Score      = 1.125^ZodiacRarity * ZodiacQuality * (9 + ZodiacLevel^2) * 2 * ((ZodiacLevel - 90) / 10) ^ 2.5
Zodiac Sell Cost  = (ZodiacScore / 10)^0.75 * 1.1^ZodiacRarity

and:
ZodiacRarity = Immo+ Number + 9
</pre>


